Firestore rules are maintained in the deployable ruleset at the repository
root: `firestore.rules`. This file is a deployment note, not a rules fragment.

The rules protect `student_directory/current` behind verified operator
accounts, retain the app's shared sports data, backup, scoreboard, and history
operations, and deny unlisted top-level Firestore collections. Writes to
`app_data` are limited to the document types used by the application.

From the repository root, deploy the complete ruleset with:

    firebase deploy --only firestore:rules --project thsportsfes

Verify the deployed rules in the Firebase Console. Only then set
`FIRESTORE_RULES_READY` to `true` in `public/student-search.js` and publish the
updated page so the private directory can be unlocked.